  "question": {
    "text": "The temperature of an ideal gas is increased from 200 K to 800 K . If r.m.s. speed of gas at 200 K is $v_0$. Then, r.m.s. speed of the gas at 800 K will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sUOLA",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{v}_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2iRu6",
      "text": "$4 v_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QKCXz",
      "text": "$\\frac{v_0}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "69sbr",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{v}_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "RMS speed,\n$\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{RT}}{\\mathrm{M}}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{mm}} \\propto \\sqrt{\\mathrm{T}}$\nHere, $\\mathrm{T}_{\\text {initiol }}=200 \\mathrm{~K}$\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{fing1}}=800 \\mathrm{~K}$\nInitial RMS speed $=\\mathrm{v}_0$\n$\\therefore \\frac{v_0}{v_{\\mathrm{rms}}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{200}{800}} \\Rightarrow v_{\\mathrm{ms}}=2 v_0$",
    "image": null
  },
